{
 "description": "Kernel-version pin (backlog #44, kernel 2.0.0). A content manifest MAY carry `kernel-version`; absent means 1.0.0 content. KERNEL-1: a bundle whose content needs a later kernel (a Risk object, Finding.risk-refs) MUST pin that kernel. KERNEL-2: a tool that meets a pin it does not implement fails closed and names the pinned version and its own. Each vector: a manifest (objects list left empty - the vector's objects are given beside it), the objects, and the expected number of failures. shape-vectors (2.0.0-rc.3): fields that 2.0.0 typed or added on released shapes - Finding.actions[].due and Deviation.opened, free text in 1.0.0 (DATE-2, DATE-1: an invalid vector names its rule in expected-rules), and Component.product-version, an opaque string; `kind` is the type the document must match exactly, or none. CP-AUTHOR-1 (2026-11-13): the pin vectors hold `provenance` on a Tailoring, an entry of it and an Implementation, `decided` and `review-due` on a Deviation and `date` on an authorization to KERNEL-1; the shape vectors hold the closed `provenance`, the new fields and the three times that any string satisfied until then (DATE-3 a Mapping's provenance date, DATE-4 an Assessment's time, DATE-5 an Attestation's timestamp; DATE-1 now names `decided` too). Backlog #68 (2026-11-13): a `pattern` of this schema is an ECMA-262 regular expression, as JSON Schema says - `$` is the end of the value and `.` matches no line terminator (U+000A, U+000D, U+2028, U+2029). The shape vectors hold a date, a date-time, a digest, a language tag, a facet id, a fact name and a decimal default that end in a line break to `invalid`, and a relation type with a line terminator after `https://`; one pin vector holds a `kernel-version` that ends in a line break to a manifest that is refused. Python's `re` and .NET's `Regex` accept each of them when a pattern is handed over unchanged.",
